  "narration": {
    "title": "Cleveland and Chicago Barge Into the Top Ten",
    "intro": "The playoff picture up top is settled, but the middle of our power ranking had a loud week. The Guardians and White Sox each won five and six games' worth of ground, respectively, and shoved their way up the board. Milwaukee, meanwhile, hasn't budged from first for a reason.",
    "power_lead": "The Brewers held the top spot at 102-59, going 5-1 behind Brice Turang's two homers and six RBI. The real climbers were the Guardians, up six spots to third after a 5-1 week and a plus-11 run differential, and the White Sox, up seven to eighth on a plus-19 week powered by Chase Meidroth's 1.470 stretch.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs edge the Dodgers for the top team OPS at .765 to .763, a gap too thin to argue about; both leave everyone else behind. Milwaukee sits third at .744, a nice pairing with the best record in the game.",
    "staffs_lead": "The Yankees own the best rotation by starter ERA at 3.30, with the Dodgers (3.42) and Rays (3.47) a step back but stingier on the bases at a 1.08 WHIP. Boston runs the best bullpen at a 2.99 ERA, the one part of the Red Sox that's held all year."
  }
